{
  "id": "arcs-sectors-radians",
  "order": 408,
  "domain": "geometry-trig",
  "skill": "circles",
  "title": "Arcs, sectors and radians",
  "minutes": 6,
  "hook": "An arc or a sector is a fraction of the whole circle: the angle over $360^{\\circ}$, or over $2\\pi$.",
  "steps": [
    {
      "type": "recall",
      "prompt": "From memory: how many radians are in $180^{\\circ}$?",
      "answer": "$\\pi$ radians."
    },
    {
      "type": "fill",
      "prompt": "Convert $60^{\\circ}$ to radians.",
      "lines": [
        "$60 \\times \\pi /180$",
        "$= \\pi /$___"
      ],
      "accept": [
        "3"
      ],
      "why": "$60/180 = 1/3$."
    },
    {
      "type": "predict",
      "prompt": "A circle has radius 6. How long is an arc with a $90^{\\circ}$ central angle?",
      "choices": [
        "$3\\pi$",
        "$6\\pi$",
        "$9\\pi$",
        "$12\\pi$"
      ],
      "answer": 0,
      "why": "$90/360$ of the circumference $12\\pi$."
    },
    {
      "type": "slider",
      "prompt": "A circle has radius 6. Drag the central angle until the sector's area is $12\\pi$.",
      "param": {
        "name": "t",
        "min": 0,
        "max": 360,
        "step": 10,
        "start": 60
      },
      "answer": 120,
      "why": "Sector $\\text{area} = (θ/360) \\times \\pi r^{2} = (θ/360) \\times 36\\pi$. That's $12\\pi$ when θ $= 120^{\\circ}$, a third of the circle.",
      "readout": "Angle: ${t}^{\\circ}$, sector area: ${=t/10}\\pi$",
      "pie": {
        "angle": "t"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "predict",
      "prompt": "Radius 10, central angle $72^{\\circ}$. What's the sector's area?",
      "choices": [
        "$20\\pi$",
        "$4\\pi$",
        "$10\\pi$",
        "$72\\pi$"
      ],
      "answer": 0,
      "why": "$72/360 = 1/5$ of $100\\pi$."
    },
    {
      "type": "predict",
      "prompt": "In radians, arc $\\text{length} =$ rθ. Radius 4 and θ $= 2.5$ radians. Arc length?",
      "choices": [
        "10",
        "6.5",
        "1.6",
        "20"
      ],
      "answer": 0,
      "why": "$4 \\times 2.5$."
    },
    {
      "type": "spot",
      "prompt": "Converting $3\\pi /4$ radians to degrees. Tap the line with the mistake.",
      "lines": [
        "$3\\pi /4 \\times 180/\\pi$",
        "$= 3 \\times 180 / 4$",
        "$= 145^{\\circ}$"
      ],
      "wrong": 2,
      "why": "$540 \\div 4 = 135^{\\circ}$."
    },
    {
      "type": "predict",
      "prompt": "An arc is $1/6$ of the circumference. Its central angle in radians is:",
      "choices": [
        "$\\pi /3$",
        "$\\pi /6$",
        "$\\pi /12$",
        "$\\pi /2$"
      ],
      "answer": 0,
      "why": "$1/6$ of $2\\pi$."
    }
  ],
  "keys": [
    "Fraction of the $\\text{circle} = \\text{angle}/360^{\\circ} = \\text{angle}/2\\pi$.",
    "$\\text{Arc} = \\text{fraction} \\times 2\\pi r$. $\\text{Sector} = \\text{fraction} \\times \\pi r^{2}$.",
    "Degrees to radians: $\\times \\pi /180$. Radians to degrees: $\\times 180/\\pi$."
  ],
  "recall": [
    {
      "type": "predict",
      "prompt": "$90^{\\circ}$ in radians is:",
      "choices": [
        "$\\pi /2$",
        "$\\pi$",
        "$\\pi /4$"
      ],
      "answer": 0,
      "why": "Half of $\\pi$."
    },
    {
      "type": "fill",
      "prompt": "Radius 3 and θ $= 2$ radians. Arc length?",
      "lines": [
        "rθ $= 3 \\times 2 =$ ___"
      ],
      "accept": [
        "6"
      ],
      "why": "rθ."
    },
    {
      "type": "predict",
      "prompt": "A semicircle's arc is what fraction of the circumference?",
      "choices": [
        "$1/2$",
        "$1/4$",
        "$1/3$"
      ],
      "answer": 0,
      "why": "180 of 360 degrees."
    }
  ],
  "format": "classic",
  "tex": true
}
